    {
      "id": "r20261109-a02",
      "title": "Why More Students Are Taking a Gap Year",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "After high school, most students go straight to university. But a growing number are choosing something different: a gap year, a break of twelve months before they continue their studies.",
        "During a gap year, students might work, travel, or volunteer. A student who teaches English in a village, for example, learns patience and leadership that no classroom can give. Many return to university with clearer goals and more maturity.",
        "Some parents worry that a gap year is just a long holiday. Research suggests otherwise: students who take a structured gap year often get better grades than those who do not. The key is having a plan, not just free time."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "gap year": "tahun jeda",
        "straight": "langsung",
        "volunteer": "menjadi relawan",
        "patience": "kesabaran",
        "maturity": "kedewasaan",
        "worry": "khawatir",
        "structured": "terencana"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "What is a gap year?",
          "opts": [
            "A year of studying abroad",
            "A year of military service",
            "A twelve-month break before university"
